@startuml Preciazo_DB_Identity_Access
title Preciazo - Identity and Access Database (AV2)
hide circle
skinparam linetype ortho

entity users {
    * id : BIGINT <<PK>>
    --
    email : VARCHAR <<UQ>>
    password_hash : VARCHAR
    status : VARCHAR
    failed_attempts : INTEGER
    locked_until : TIMESTAMP <<NULLABLE>>
    security_check_required : BOOLEAN
    version : BIGINT
}

entity roles {
    * id : BIGINT <<PK>>
    --
    name : VARCHAR <<UQ>>
}

entity permissions {
    * id : BIGINT <<PK>>
    --
    resource : VARCHAR
    action : VARCHAR
}

entity user_roles {
    * user_id : BIGINT <<PK, FK>>
    * role_id : BIGINT <<PK, FK>>
}

entity role_permissions {
    * role_id : BIGINT <<PK, FK>>
    * permission_id : BIGINT <<PK, FK>>
}

users ||--o{ user_roles
roles ||--o{ user_roles
roles ||--o{ role_permissions
permissions ||--o{ role_permissions

note right of users
  Canonical case-insensitive email is unique; password_hash stores encoded hash only.
  failed_attempts >= 0; version protects concurrent login state changes.
  Threshold failure sets a future locked_until and security_check_required=true.
  Expiry alone does not clear the security-check requirement.
  Persist failed attempts even when authentication returns an error Result.
  No password, security proof or token is stored in plaintext.
  Stateless JWT: no auth_sessions, refresh-token or token-revocation table.
end note

note right of permissions
  UNIQUE(resource, action); user_roles and role_permissions have composite PKs.
  Startup seed is idempotent, preserves ids and never drops existing assignments.
  Public personas map to allowlisted BUYER / MERCHANT memberships only.
  No baseline persona grants privileged price-reports:resolve.
  Every new user has at least one seeded role; validated in registration transaction.
end note

@enduml
